)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Commands -- FIND, more                   !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  Examples:
{    F IEF404I              }the next line with IEF404I
{    F JOB PREV             }the line before with JOB
{    F 'NOT CATLGD' ALL     }how often it occurs, and the first
{    F X'5B' 1              }a dollar sign in column 1
{    F ABEND 20 60          }ABEND within columns 20 to 60
}
}  On the log and on output, one FIND looks through FINDLIM lines at most
}  (5000 unless set otherwise, topic 10 of the commands) and then says
}  FINDLIM REACHED; the next FIND goes on from there.
}
}  The last string is kept: in the next SDSF session, FIND alone or PF5
}  looks for it again.
}
}  Mistakes: INVALID HEX STRING, INCONSISTENT PARAMETERS (two directions,
}  two kinds, or a string longer than the columns), INVALID LEFT BOUNDARY
}  and INVALID RIGHT BOUNDARY.
}
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: commands   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFKSCR
  &ZUP = ISFKALL
)END
